VBLTEST(1)                       User Commands                      VBLTEST(1)

NAME
       vbltest - measure the display manager's vertical-blank rate

SYNOPSIS
       vbltest [options]

DESCRIPTION
       vbltest  asks  the kernel's display manager for a vertical-blank event,
       waits for it, asks for the next one, and every five seconds prints  the
       rate  it  is getting.  It is the shortest answer to "are vertical-blank
       events arriving, and at what frequency", which is the question behind a
       session that tears, stutters, or never repaints at all.

       The number to expect on this system is 60 Hz: the kernel's  driver  has
       no  vertical-blank interrupt from the emulated device and generates the
       events from a high-resolution timer instead, which is what  the  refer-
       ence  driver does on the same hardware.  A rate that drifts far from 60
       says the timer is not firing when it should, not that  the  display  is
       misconfigured.

       Reading  events needs no master rights, so this can run while X has the
       display.

OPTIONS
       -D device
              Open the given device node instead of searching.

       -M module
              Open the node  belonging  to  the  named  driver,  for  instance
              vmwgfx.

       -s     Wait on the secondary pipe rather than the first.

SEE ALSO
       drminfo(1), modetest(1), proptest(1)

